by ousamabenyounes at 2026-05-01T23:02:44Z

Reproduced the bug locally — sharing the exact steps so reviewers can verify the regression and the fix without running PHPUnit.

### Environment

- Docker image: `php:8.4-cli` (`PHP 8.4.20 (cli) (built: Apr 22 2026 01:24:37) (NTS)`)
- libxml: PHP-bundled
- Tmp dir with a space in its name: `/tmp/dir with space/` (mimics a Windows user profile such as `C:\Users\John Doe\AppData\Local\Temp`)
- No Symfony bootstrap — pure libxml repro of the failing call site (`DOMDocument::schemaValidateSource()` with the `xsd:include` schema produced inside `XliffUtils::shouldEnableEntityLoader()`)

### Repro script

```php
<?php
$tmpfile = tempnam('/tmp/dir with space', 'symfony');
file_put_contents($tmpfile, '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<xsd:schema xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <xsd:element name="test" type="testType" />
  <xsd:complexType name="testType"/>
</xsd:schema>');

set_error_handler(function ($severity, $message) {
    if (!(error_reporting() & $severity)) {
        echo "  [SILENCED] severity=$severity msg=$message\n";
        return true;
    }
    return false;
});

function probe(string $label, string $schema): void {
    echo "=== $label ===\n";
    $dom = new DOMDocument();
    $dom->loadXML('<?xml version="1.0"?><test/>');
    @$dom->schemaValidateSource($schema);
    echo "(end)\n";
}

// BEFORE patch — raw concat (current code on 6.4)
$beforeSchema = '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<xsd:schema xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <xsd:include schemaLocation="file:///'.str_replace('\\', '/', $tmpfile).'" />
</xsd:schema>';

// AFTER patch — rawurlencode segments
$parts = explode('/', str_replace('\\', '/', $tmpfile));
$drive = '\\' === DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR ? array_shift($parts).'/' : '';
$encodedUrl = 'file:///'.$drive.implode('/', array_map('rawurlencode', $parts));
$afterSchema = '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<xsd:schema xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <xsd:include schemaLocation="'.$encodedUrl.'" />
</xsd:schema>';

probe('BEFORE patch', $beforeSchema);
probe('AFTER  patch', $afterSchema);
unlink($tmpfile);
```

### Run

```bash
docker run --rm -v /tmp:/tmp php:8.4-cli php /tmp/repro-63253.php
```

### Output

```
=== BEFORE patch ===
  [SILENCED] severity=2 msg=DOMDocument::schemaValidateSource(): Internal error: xmlSchemaParseIncludeOrRedefine, could not build an URI from the schemaLocation.
  [SILENCED] severity=2 msg=DOMDocument::schemaValidateSource(): Internal error: xmlSchemaParse, An internal error occurred.
  [SILENCED] severity=2 msg=DOMDocument::schemaValidateSource(): Invalid Schema
(end)
=== AFTER  patch ===
(end)
```

The third silenced warning — `DOMDocument::schemaValidateSource(): Invalid Schema` — is the exact message reported in the issue. Symfony's `ErrorHandler` picks up `@`-silenced warnings via `set_error_handler` and routes them through `SilencedErrorContext`, which is what `stof` was hinting at: it is the error handler configuration that surfaces these as log entries despite the `@`.

### Test that captures this in PHPUnit

The branch already had a helper-level data-provider test (`testGetTmpFileUrlEncodesPathSegments`); I just added an integration test that goes through libxml itself:

`testEncodedUrlPreventsLibxmlInvalidSchemaErrors` creates a tmp dir whose name contains a space, runs `DOMDocument::schemaValidateSource()` on a schema that includes the file via the encoded URL (no errors expected) and via the raw-concat URL (errors expected). The assertion fails when the patch is reverted, with libxml emitting:

```
xmlSchemaParseIncludeOrRedefine, could not build an URI from the schemaLocation.
xmlSchemaParse, An internal error occurred.
```

Branch was force-pushed with the new integration test on top of the original patch.

