by ousamabenyounes at 2026-05-03T04:57:40Z

Iterated on the test in two follow-up commits (no change to the production fix).

The first attempt rewrote the test as a single end-to-end run through `validateSchema()`, gated by `@runInSeparateProcess` and `putenv("TMPDIR=...")` to relocate the temp dir under a path with spaces. Empirical run revealed that `sys_get_temp_dir()` caches its return on first read, so neither approach actually changes the path the test exercises — the "regression test" would stay green even with the fix reverted.

Replaced with two independent tests: a data-provider asserting the helper's encoding output, and a libxml smoke test that builds the encoded URL inline (no coupling to the helper's name) and asserts no `Invalid Schema` PHP warning nor libxml URI-parsing error is emitted. Both pipelines were verified to fire on the buggy raw URL and stay silent on the encoded one. Dropped the fragile negative assertion on the raw URL.
